{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_4eb01200602bd0e1f31189d1da89bd20e620773886f1a0a20ca864cefea21175"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Rosetta instructs agents to maintain agents/MEMORY.md with root causes, actions tried, and lessons learned, and to write execution state (plans, specs, phase progress) to disk so failed sessions resume from checkpoints."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6df9278939c44de68587a51f6d4f3e1e51da591d07473526e15f3d36075116b8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are directed to CONTRIBUTING.md for workflow and expectations, and the README notes Rosetta plugins are used to develop Rosetta itself."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8eade8d12226e253020c6117624af82638cf535978585b125b1f0afac9857104"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Rosetta layers instructions at runtime — core, then organization, then project — with higher layers propagating to every project automatically, all authored in markdown and versioned in Git."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c374efadca4a55f60dd11be885721d7ab3de18810307d689ba084426a5ea9374"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Rosetta ships named workflows including coding-flow, requirements-authoring-flow, security-flow, testgen/api-aqa/ui-aqa flows, and code-analysis-flow, each with defined phases, subagents, and HITL gates."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eef3808ac163ac4403de73bf68064633c76426344aeb8884abd6190b40ae485e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Rosetta workflows instruct the agent to delegate review to a separate subagent with a fresh context window that inspects the implementation against original specs, and to use a validator subagent with real execution evidence."}],"claim_ids":["clm_4eb01200602bd0e1f31189d1da89bd20e620773886f1a0a20ca864cefea21175","clm_6df9278939c44de68587a51f6d4f3e1e51da591d07473526e15f3d36075116b8","clm_8eade8d12226e253020c6117624af82638cf535978585b125b1f0afac9857104","clm_c374efadca4a55f60dd11be885721d7ab3de18810307d689ba084426a5ea9374","clm_eef3808ac163ac4403de73bf6806